Domain: music theory

Focus on: notes, intervals, chords, scales, keys & harmonic functions

notes --> intervals --> chords --> harmonic functions

scales and keys form context for chords 

Notes:
7 basic notes: C, D, E, F, G, A, B

Interval:
Distance between two notes: 
e.g. from C to D = Major Second; from C to Db = Minor Second from C to E = Major Third; from C to F = Perfect Fourth

Chords:
Combination of multiple notes that are simultaneously being played
e.g. triad: a chord with 3 different notes --> e.g. C, E, G
types: Major, Minor, Dimiished, Augmented
combination of intervals determine what chord it is

Scales:
a collection of notes that are organised according to a certain structure
e.g. C Major Scale: C-D-E-F-G-A-B-C
